1.3.1
-----------------
Updated: The Import management tab shows an icon in the admin header (Icon=upload in menu.ini [Topmenu_sqliimport], drawn by the admin4 design)
Fixed: The extension loads and runs on PHP 8: a string offset written with braces (a parse error since PHP 8.0) in SQLICSVRowSet,
       the universal getters of SQLIImportItem and SQLIScheduledImport declare the mixed return type of the kernel's persistent object,
       the Iterator, ArrayAccess and Countable methods carry ReturnTypeWillChange, nullable parameters are declared explicitly (PHP 8.4),
       and SQLIScheduledImport::__toString() always returns a string
Updated: README.md replaces README.rst: requirements, installation with Composer and by hand, every setting, the admin pages,
         the command line script and cronjobs, writing a handler, the content API, permissions, upgrading and troubleshooting
Updated: composer.json is se7enxweb/sqliimport (replacing lolautruche/sqliimport), requires PHP 8.0 or later and states the support links;
         ezinfo.php is new; ezinfo.php and extension.xml state version 1.3.1, the license and the website

1.3.0, 1.2.x
-----------------
See the tags at https://github.com/se7enxweb/sqliimport/tags (PostgreSQL schema, no output to STDERR, earlier fixes).

1.2.1
-----------------
Added Oracle schema (Thanks Simone Tellini !)
Updated doc about content options and publish options - http://bit.ly/f3f2RI
Fixed issue : Datatypes fromString() / toString() always appear consistent, even if they are not implemented - http://bit.ly/f3f2RI
Fixed "Using $this in a non object context in sqlilocation" - http://bit.ly/fzJN8G
Fixed issue with SQLICSVDoc::parse() : Didn't return csv doc object - http://bit.ly/dbphvq
SQLIContentUtils::getRemoteFile() : Added a parameter indicating whether to allow proxy use or not, allowing to override proxy settings from site.ini
Fixed issue with csv row iteration, throwing an SQLICSVException (Thanks Edi Modrić !)

1.2.0
-----------------
Implemented feature : SIGTERM and SIGINT calls are now caught and import is smoothly and safely interrupted (PCNTL extension needed)
Fixed issue : Scheduled imports - schedule is shifting - http://bit.ly/cJPe5F
Fixed issue : Editing a scheduled import may add empty options - http://bit.ly/bXYAPH
Scheduled imports are now linked from import list


1.1.0
-----------------
Added manual frequency support for scheduled imports (not less than every 5 minutes)
Added import duration monitor
Fixed issue : Imports are blocked after a transaction error
Fixed some i18n issues
Fixed a notice in SQLIImportHandlerOptions::__toString()

1.0.3
-----------------
Fixed a notice in SQLIImportFactory::cleanup()
Fixed issue with section assignement on new sqli content object - http://bit.ly/aD8O61
Implemented shorthand method to easily handle HTML in content API

1.0.2
-----------------
Fixed issue : Exception thrown when setting a RobotUserID

1.0.1
-----------------
Fixed issue : Content creation with non-default language - http://bit.ly/9iNxyb
Fixed issue : Parent location doesn't update in publisher
Implemented "defaultLocation" in SQLIContent. You can now get the default location, corresponding to content 'main_node' : $defaultLocation = $sqliContent->defaultLocation; // returns SQLILocation

